getfem
------------------------------------------
GetFEM is an open source library based on collaborative development. It aims to
offer the most flexible framework for solving potentially coupled systems of
linear and nonlinear partial differential equations with the finite element
method. It works in arbitrary dimension and allows to couple 1D, 2D and 3D
problems.

Runtime requirements:
  bash-5.2.21-1
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libgetfem5-5.5-1bl1
  liblapack0-3.12.0-1
  libqhull_8-2020.2-1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  libsuperlu7-7.0.1-1bl2

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-20260320-3
  automake-20261107-1
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  liblapack-devel-3.12.0-1
  libqhull-devel-2020.2-1
  libsuperlu-devel-7.0.1-1bl2
  libtool-2.6.2-1
  make-4.4.1-2

Canonical website:
  https://getfem.org/

Canonical download:
  mirror://savannah/getfem/stable/getfem-5.5.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack getfem-5.5-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./getfem-5.5-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/getfem-5.5-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/getfem-5.5-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libgetfem5-5.5-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libgetfem-devel-5.5-X.tar.xz

